Project context for mock3:
- Two codelines are in scope: mocka (fare engine, src/fares.ts + test/fares.test.ts) and mockb (departure board, src/schedule.ts + test/schedule.test.ts). Both use vitest (`vitest run`) and TypeScript (`tsc --noEmit`).
- Both in-scope defects are boundary-condition bugs:
  - MOCK3-1 (mocka): `fareFor` uses `rider.age > 65` instead of `>= 65`, so riders aged exactly 65 are charged the adult fare. The existing test covers age 70 but not age 65 — a coverage gap at the exact boundary.
